+++
title: The desk doesn't need to be tidy
coach: sam
date: 2025-04-10
domains: creativity
teaser: A desk that looks like active work is happening on it is doing exactly what it's supposed to do.
+++

<img src="../img/whisper-sams-desk.jpg" alt="Sam's writing desk, cluttered with notebooks and loose pages" class="content-photo content-photo-right">

Clients apologize for their desk before I've even asked about it. The
stack of half-filled notebooks, the sticky notes that don't mean
anything anymore, the draft printed out and marked up in three different
colors of pen.

None of that is the problem. A desk that looks like active work is
happening on it is doing exactly what it's supposed to do. The tidy
desk — the one kept clear for when you're "really ready to start" — is
usually the one nothing gets written at.

Let the desk be evidence, not a waiting room.
